WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.090
Some American cities have buses.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.340
Some use trams and trains.
And there's one...

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.410
that uses golf carts.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.040
- My name is Vanessa Fleisch

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.480
and I am the mayor of
Peachtree City, Georgia.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:21.370
It's a small city of about 35,000 people
that is about 20 minutes south of Atlanta.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.950
It's asphalt paths, we have
over 100 miles of them.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:30.020
They range from 8 feet to
10 feet wide in some places.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:33.040
They're used for golf carts mostly.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.180
We have over 11,000 registered
golf carts in the city.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.860
Obviously, pedestrians, bicyclists,
all kinds of traffic is on these paths.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.690
Morning!

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.520
- You do have to register them?
- Yes, you do.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.820
The people in the city do register them.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.010
- There's someone else approaching us now.
I assume it's like regular roads.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.540
You pass on the right and...

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.480
- Correct.
- Yeah?

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.080
- Yeah.
- It's a parallel road network, basically.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.050
- The majority of the city
is accessible by carts

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.760
and that's a huge attraction
because parents

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.970
can pick up their kids at
school if they want to.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.220
- And some of the kids
can drive themselves?

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:19.190
- Yes, the younger kids or the sophomores
at the local high schools are allowed

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:23.070
with their learner's permit to
drive their carts to school.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:23.900
- Wow.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.070
- It's a bit of freedom that they enjoy.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.390
- And I guess if it's
limited to 20 miles an hour,

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.570
there's less of a chance of a bad bump.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.460
So, this is the high school.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.290
- This is.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:39.270
There's parking at the
high school for 615 carts.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.210
- That is a lot of golf carts.
Do all the students leave at once here?

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.400
Is it just a traffic jam of golf carts?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.400
- It is a traffic jam of golf carts
and it's not always pretty.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.230
- Some of them have a limiter?

00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:53.520
- They do, but sometimes
they can be removed

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.240
and they go faster than they
should, which isn't good.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.130
- No, that's exactly what I'd have done
at age 15 with my own golf cart.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.360
I would have removed the limiter on it.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.490
- Some of the carts have
heaters inside them and radios.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.670
You can soup them up as
much as you want really.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.500
After they saw the popularity
in the '70s what they did

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.120
was they required, whenever there was
a new subdivision of houses built,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.200
that they connected the paths.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:25.050
For the most part, the
cart paths are laid out

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.050
at the same time they lay out the roads.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:28.830
- So, what are the road rules here?

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.770
It's like you're in a regular vehicle,

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:31.680
you've just got more
paths that you can go on?

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.130
- Yes, and if there is no path,

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.820
you are allowed to be on
the road, but that's why

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.180
we've expanded the paths
because we're trying

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.300
to keep people off of
them as much as possible.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.550
Sometimes people who have never
been here have been caught

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.980
on cart paths with their cars

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.130
thinking that that's the right thing to do.
- Wow!

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.580
- I wanted to take you through a drive-thru.
So up here is McDonald's.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.440
- I'm still getting over the fact
that I'm in a drive-thru in a golf cart!

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.960
- Thank you.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.010
- Should point out, not sponsored.
This is not product placement.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.770
- The brakes on this are very good.
I'm sorry, it's very abrupt on them.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.460
- Better than the alternative.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.700
Peachtree City was a
planned community, right?

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.220
- Correct.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.580
- How did it go from
"we're gonna build some houses here"

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.780
to we're gonna have something that

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.520
that I don't think any
other city in America has?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:28.420
- It got started originally
as a lake retreat for Atlanta residents.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:32.640
And the people who were here,
basically only on the weekends,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:39.300
they started taking their golf carts on the roads
leaving from playing golf.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.420
This whole separate network
came up as a result of that

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.420
to get them off the
roads on their way home.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.220
- So, this was founded in the 1950s.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.960
- 1959 by Joel Cowan.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:59.880
He was a college student
when he designed and founded this city.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.420
- Wow.
- It's very quiet...

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.720
See what I mean?

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:08.460
- Death wish, good grief!

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:12.200
- Along here, this is Lake Peachtree--

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.860
- Sorry, I got distracted by ducks.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.660
- The Founder, Mr. Cowan
and his cousin were the ones

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.590
that put up the dam
and spillway originally

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.880
that made this lake.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:28.380
100,000 gallons a second goes over this.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:32.460
People do pay taxes to
pay towards these roads.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.700
It costs us $1.8 million a
year to maintain what we have

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.880
as well as the 29 bridges and 29 tunnels.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.920
- This is a pretty affluent
city, which I guess is one

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.820
of the reasons that the
golf cart paths work,

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.310
but there are a lot of
cities like that in America

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:53.740
and I'm trying to work
out why it's worked here

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.320
and it hasn't elsewhere.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.700
- Most mayors when they see or
hear about us and they think

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.640
"oh, we can do that", well,
they've got older cities,

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.320
so they really can't.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.540
- And I guess part of it is cost.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:12.440
Part of it is you need a
huge amount of upkeep and tax

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:15.790
and everything to make this
work, but it's also because

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:20.130
you need to set the whole
thing up or it doesn't work.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.560
You can't have a quarter of a cart network

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.720
because no one will buy a
cart and no one will use it.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.820
You need to connect everything
or it's not worth it.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:29.720
- Right.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.940
- Lovely! Thank you very much.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:33.840
- Thank you.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.070
- You can find out more about
Peachtree City in the links in the description.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.890
I've just realised there's
no seat belts on this.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:48.720
- No.

